  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit and maximum uncertainty about the performance landscape. The best first step is to establish a clean, minimal RNA-only baseline (single profile, PCA n2000) that isolates the RNA signal without confounding from image modality, aggregation, or fusion. This single experiment answers: what is the performance floor for RNA data with a standard linear encoder? It is the simplest possible configuration, reducing the chance of implementation issues, and provides the reference accuracy needed to judge whether more complex choices (learned encoders, multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation) actually add value. With 9 experiments remaining, this baseline will anchor all subsequent comparisons and help prioritize which design axes (encoder quality, modality, aggregation) are worth exploring next."
